                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab^{op} \to CompAb
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CompAb
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CompAb^{op} \to Ab
          %p
            where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            is the category of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+space"}> discrete topological
            ) groups and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CompAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CompAb
            is the category of abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+groups"} compact topological groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LocCompAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LocCompAb
            in the evident way.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
            on abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+groups"} locally compact groups
            is formulated in terms of Pontrjagin duals (see below).
          %h3#BasicPropertiesOfDualGroups Basic properties of dual groups
          %p
            There are many properties of Hausdorff abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+groups"} locally compact groups
            that implies properties of their Pontrjagin duals. For example:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is finite.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
              %p
                (see also at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nearby+homomorphisms+from+compact+Lie+groups+are+conjugate"} nearby homomorphisms from compact Lie groups are conjugate
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "-free" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+group"} torsion group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat A
                is an abelian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite group
                (for more see at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+duality+for+torsion+abelian+groups"} Pontryagin duality for torsion abelian groups
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is
                = succeed "-free" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is compactly generated in that there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood"} neighborhood
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
                that generates
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                as a group.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is compactly generated, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is a Lie group.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+countable+topological+space"} second countable
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is second countable.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+topological+space"} separable
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrizable+topological+space"} metrizable
          %p
            For a discussion of these facts see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Morris77"} Morris 77
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Armacost81"} Armacost 81
          %ul
            %li
              Variations on Pontryagin duality, (
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/11/variations_on_pontryagin_duali.html"}> nCafe
              )
          %p
            Another statement of this type is presented in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Mackey48"} Mackey 1948
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is connected if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
              is a product of a discrete torsion-free group with a finite dimensional real vector space.
          %h2#applications Applications
          %p
            Pontrjagin duality underlies the abstract framework of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+analysis"} Fourier analysis
            on locally compact Hausdorff abelian groups
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mover
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_A: L^2(A, d\mu) \to L^2(\hat{A}, d\hat{\mu})\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\mu
            is a suitable choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haar+measure"} Haar measure
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mover
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\hat{\mu}
            is a suitable choice of Haar measure on the dual group. Fourier duality is compatible with Pontrjagin duality in the sense that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{\hat{A}}
            is identified with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_{\hat{A}}
            is the inverse of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_A
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+duality+for+torsion+abelian+groups"} Pontryagin duality for torsion abelian groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+group"} locally compact topological group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character+group"} character group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartier+duality"}> Cartier duality
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+line+bundle"} Poincaré line bundle
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Pontrjagin34
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theory of topological commutative groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968438"} doi:10.2307/1968438
              %p
                Russian translation: Uspekhi Mat. Nauk, 1936, no. 2, 177–195 (
                %a{:href => "http://mi.mathnet.ru/eng/umn8882"}> mathnet:umn8882
                )
          %p Gentle exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              Partha Sarathi Chakraborty,
              %em Pontrjagin duality for finite groups
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Chakraborty_PontrjaginDuality.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Morris77
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sidney+A.+Morris"}> Sidney A. Morris
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Pontryagin Duality and the Structure of Locally Compact Abelian Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511600722"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511600722
            %li#Armacost81
              %p
                David L. Armacost,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Structure of Locally Compact Abelian Groups
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pontryagin_duality"} Pontryagin duality
          %p Also:
          %ul
            %li#Mackey48
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Mackey"}> George Mackey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Laplace Transform For Locally Compact Abelian Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/87968"} jstor:87968
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                ,
                %em On duality of topological abelian groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/ftp/pdffiles/abgp.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr_PontrjaginDuality.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p which provides a perhaps better context for Pontryagin duality than the category of locally compact Hausdorff abelian groups (also known as ‘LCA groups’). Barr explains:
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Did you know that there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+category"} *-autonomous category
                  of topological abelian groups that includes all the LCA groups and whose duality extends that of Pontrjagin? The groups are characterized by the property that among all topological groups on the same underlying abelian group and with the same set of continuous homomorphisms to the circle, these have the finest topology. It is not obvious that such a finest exists, but it does and that is the key.
          %h3#for_higher_groups For higher groups
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            Pontrjagin duality for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groups"} 2-groups
            and application to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
          %ul
            %li#BSST07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schick"} Thomas Schick
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Spitzweck"} Markus Spitzweck
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Thom"} Andreas Thom
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality for topological abelian group stacks and T-duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0701428"} arXiv:math/0701428
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calder+Daenzer"}> Calder Daenzer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A groupoid approach to noncommutative T-duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.upenn.edu/grad/dissertations/DaenzerThesis.pdf"} pdf
